      "side": 1,
      "message": "SSE is a long-lived stream where the client only receives, and the QUIC codec built at in HTTPClient.connectQuic() sets no maxIdleTimeout, so the underlying QUIC library keeps its default of 0(disabled); HTTPServer.buildQuicCodec() omits it too. If the server host vanishes without a CONNECTION_CLOSE nothing notices: channelInactive never fires, onStreamEnd() is never called, and the subscription\nsilently stops delivering, where HTTP/2 is covered by TCPClient\u0027s keepalives. Could we set maxIdleTimeout from quic-client-parameters?",
      "revId": "84940f7d9f35554d8b327dcf7a39964ea94f803a",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
